## CURRENT STATE

- `frontend/` + `backend/` remain the served product. The public
  `frontend-next/` beta is separate and is not the Phase 13 cutover.
- D1 Account Seller Overview is CLOSED. PR #90 was merged into `main` at
  `df5265d09fbec7723aab406187a828fa3854f653`, the D2 branch baseline.
- Production project ref `pijnmcllmfgjmgsvtcej` is `ACTIVE_HEALTHY` on
  PostgreSQL 17. The read-only migration ledger audit directly confirms
  `20260825180000 public_profile_foundation`; the prior D8 uncertainty is
  resolved. D2 migration `20260826120000` is not in that ledger before ship.
- D2 adds `public.wine_regions` with the 17 current `/esplora` region names,
  excluding the UI pseudo-value `Tutte`, and deterministic data-defined order.
  A unique index on `lower(nome)` prevents logical case-insensitive duplicates.
  `anon` and `authenticated` receive `SELECT` only through an explicit RLS
  policy; no client write grant exists.
- The migration changes only the two authorized legacy values: every exact
  `Toscanaa` becomes `Toscana`; exact `ciao` becomes `Emilia-Romagna` only for
  `slug = 'sabbioni-i-rifugi-2017'`. A residual-value gate aborts before the
  constraint if any other noncanonical value exists.
- `wines.regione` remains `text NOT NULL` and `wines_regione_idx` remains in
  place. The foreign key to `wine_regions(nome)` is added `NOT VALID` and then
  explicitly validated, with `ON UPDATE CASCADE` and `ON DELETE RESTRICT`.
  Existing grants and RLS policies for `wines`, `bottle_units` and `listings`
  are unchanged.
- The authoritative `/vendi` chain remains `CellarService.aggiungiBottiglia()`
  -> `public.cellar_bottiglia_aggiungi()` ->
  `private.catalogo_risolvi_vino_utente(...)`. The private writer now validates
  the submitted region before reusing an existing wine, resolves outer
  whitespace and case to the exact registry spelling, and raises readable
  `P0001` for unknown values instead of exposing a raw FK/PostgreSQL error. Its
  schema-qualified canonical helper has `search_path = ''` and is not
  executable by `public`, `anon` or `authenticated`.
- `WineRegionsService` is a minimal server/client-compatible read adapter. It
  accepts an injected Supabase client, reads only `wine_regions`, orders by
  `(ordine, nome)`, returns `Result<string[]>` and sanitizes failures. No Region
  UI is connected: `/vendi`, `/esplora`, text search and AI suggestions remain
  unchanged.
- The fresh disposable PostgreSQL 17 proof applied the pre-D2 migration chain,
  D2 fixtures and migration, then produced **25 PASSA / 0 FALLISCE**. It proved
  the exact seed and order, duplicate prevention, fail-closed access, the two
  authorized updates only, stable wine/bottle/listing IDs and relationships,
  preserved listing history, the validated FK/index/nullability, canonical and
  rejected writer paths, unchanged ACL/RLS, and a closed helper door. Cleanup
  left zero fixture users, profiles, wines, bottle units, listings or orphan
  price observations; the append-only guard was enabled. The grid was never run
  in production.
- The D2 targeted Bun 1.3.14 test produced **16 pass / 0 fail / 61 expect()
  calls**. The full `frontend-next` suite produced **909 pass / 0 fail / 17,973
  expect() calls** across 56 files, so CI `MIN_TESTS` and its source-contract
  test are raised from 893 to the measured 909. Lint has zero errors and 13
  pre-existing unrelated warnings; typecheck and build are clean.
- The privileged read-only production precheck matched the Cabina snapshot
  exactly: 12 wines distributed as `Champagne` 1, `ciao` 1,
  `Emilia-Romagna` 1, `Lombardia` 1, `Piemonte` 3, `Toscana` 4 and
  `Toscanaa` 1, with no additional nonmappable region. I Rifugi remains `ciao`
  with one bottle unit and two listings; the QA wine remains `Toscanaa` with one
  bottle unit and no listing. The local temporary dump used for this narrow
  audit was deleted.
- No production row was inserted, updated, deleted or recreated during BUILD or
  pre-ship verification. No production fixture or migration application was
  performed. No Region UI, provider, payment, payout, Phase 11 or Phase 13 work
  was introduced. The unrelated `.wslconfig`, stash and other worktrees remain
  excluded and untouched.

